Audit the entire project for responsiveness issues and improve the UI across all screen sizes.

Requirements:
- Check every page, component, modal, navbar, sidebar, form, card, table, button, and section.
- Test responsiveness for:
  - Mobile (320px, 375px, 390px)
  - Tablet (768px, 1024px)
  - Laptop (1280px, 1440px)
  - Large screens (1920px+)

Fix:
- Overflow issues (horizontal scrolling, clipped content)
- Elements going outside the viewport
- Incorrect spacing, padding, and margins
- Text wrapping problems
- Buttons becoming too small or overlapping
- Images/cards not scaling properly
- Navbar and sidebar behavior on smaller screens
- Tables and complex layouts on mobile
- Forms and input fields responsiveness
- Modals/dialogs fitting properly on all devices

Design improvements:
- Do not just shrink desktop layouts; create proper mobile-first responsive layouts.
- Maintain a premium, modern SaaS-style UI.
- Add smooth responsive transitions and animations where appropriate.
- Improve spacing hierarchy and visual balance.
- Make layouts feel intentional on every screen size.
- Use creative but consistent design patterns (subtle gradients, glass effects, background shapes, modern cards, micro-interactions) while keeping the existing brand identity.
- Avoid generic responsive fixes; make the UI feel polished and unique.

For each issue:
1. Identify the component/page causing the problem.
2. Explain the issue briefly.
3. Apply the fix directly.
4. Ensure no existing functionality breaks.

After completing:
- Run through all routes/pages.
- Verify dark/light mode compatibility if available.
- Verify accessibility (readable text sizes, touch-friendly buttons).
- Summarize all responsiveness improvements made.